From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aio: do not drop reqs_active twice for cancelled requests

aio_complete() decrements ctx->reqs_active in the KIOCB_CANCELLED branch and
then again at put_rq, which every request passes through. A cancelled
request therefore takes the counter down by two for the one increment in
aio_get_req(). With the eight reads adbd keeps queued on FunctionFS,
free_ioctx() would see reqs_active reach zero after half of the cancelled
requests have completed, free the ring and the kioctx while the remaining
completions still dereference it, and then trip
WARN_ON(reqs_active < 0).

The only users of cancellation in this tree are gadgetfs and FunctionFS.
Let cancelled requests take the common decrement at put_rq.
---
--- a/fs/aio.c
+++ b/fs/aio.c
@@ -621,8 +621,11 @@
 	 */
 	if (unlikely(xchg(&iocb->ki_cancel,
 			  KIOCB_CANCELLED) == KIOCB_CANCELLED)) {
-		atomic_dec(&ctx->reqs_active);
-		/* Still need the wake_up in case free_ioctx is waiting */
+		/*
+		 * reqs_active is dropped at put_rq below, like for any other
+		 * request. Still need the wake_up in case free_ioctx is
+		 * waiting.
+		 */
 		goto put_rq;
 	}
 
